<section class="about-container section-block">
  <article class="about-section">
    <div class="about__content">
      <h2>Our Origin Story</h2>
      <p>Professional Project Partners — what we affectionately now call P3 — was founded in 2003 in Des Moines, Iowa. We quickly revolutionized the staff augmentation market in the Midwest by developing quality partnerships and long-lasting relationships. We created an intimate employment process for both clients and candidates.</p>
      <p>P3’s core recruiting expertise was always in software development and product delivery, so in 2020, P3 created a subdivision called Uplift Delivery. This mighty team expanded the company’s capabilities by introducing custom software development and product delivery services.</p>
    </div>
    <img class="about__image" src="#" alt="The original garage where Professional Project Partners started" loading="lazy">
  </article>

  <article class="about-section">
    <div class="about__content">
      <h2>Our Evolution</h2>
      <p>P3+Uplift was born four years later in 2024 when P3 and Uplift Delivery officially merged their talents, creating a comprehensive “one-stop-shop” to capitalize on our diverse range of service offerings. While our roots originated in the local marketplace, over the last two decades P3+Uplift’s services have expanded across the nation.</p>
    </div>
    <img class="about__image" src="#"  alt="The previous P3 headquarters in West Des Moines"  loading="lazy">
  </article>

  <article class="about-section">
    <div class="about__content">
      <h2>Our Future</h2>
      <p>We are dedicated to revolutionizing talent and tech delivery solutions through a steadfast commitment to collaboration. The key to our growth and success isn’t complicated. It all comes down to + (plus).</p>
      <strong>Communication + Partnership + Innovation + Value</strong>
    </div>
    <img class="about__image" src="#"  alt="The current building where P3+Uplift is located in downtown Des Moines"  loading="lazy">
  </article>
</section>

